+# 19/H001: Audited baseline test renames
+
+## What upstream changed
+LLVM 19 renamed eight tests documented by T001/T003: four exact vp.splice relocations, two exact spelling corrections, and updated inline assembly and saturating truncation tests. Every destination PASSes round 1.
+
+## Why this is equivalent
+Optional --baseline-renames maps only missing baseline PASS identities to candidate PASS identities, carrying full upstream SHA-1 provenance in the report. Duplicate sources/destinations, self mappings, chains, non-baseline sources, present sources and missing/non-PASS destinations fail closed. Candidate failures and fork inventory checks remain independent. lit.sh accepts the file as optional sixth argument; default behavior is unchanged. Hash syntax is checked mechanically; provenance semantics require independent review.
+
+## What breaks if this is wrong
+Wrong identity evidence could misattribute coverage. Tests exercise valid mapping, missing/failed/skipped destinations, invalid evidence, duplicates, present sources, unrelated failures and fork inventory preservation. All 18 harness tests and bash -n pass. The real round-1 comparison drops from fourteen to six problems, removing precisely eight stale identities; all six failures remain.
+
+## Upstream reference
+- `7855703194232a94d321dceea27b45cee0c91f73`: `llvm/test/CodeGen/RISCV/vp-splice.ll` -> `llvm/test/CodeGen/RISCV/rvv/vp-splice.ll`
+- `7855703194232a94d321dceea27b45cee0c91f73`: `llvm/test/CodeGen/RISCV/vp-splice-fixed-vectors.ll` -> `llvm/test/CodeGen/RISCV/rvv/vp-splice-fixed-vectors.ll`
+- `7855703194232a94d321dceea27b45cee0c91f73`: `llvm/test/CodeGen/RISCV/vp-splice-mask-vectors.ll` -> `llvm/test/CodeGen/RISCV/rvv/vp-splice-mask-vectors.ll`
+- `7855703194232a94d321dceea27b45cee0c91f73`: `llvm/test/CodeGen/RISCV/vp-splice-mask-fixed-vectors.ll` -> `llvm/test/CodeGen/RISCV/rvv/vp-splice-mask-fixed-vectors.ll`
+- `10a55caccf4e2d397f94c1455b93d774591be45f`: `llvm/test/CodeGen/RISCV/inline-asm-S-constraint.ll` -> `llvm/test/CodeGen/RISCV/inline-asm-s-constraint.ll`
+- `b13f799616939933373610c7458687ae88fa414d`: `llvm/test/CodeGen/RISCV/rvv/fixed-vectors-fround-costrained-sdnode.ll` -> `llvm/test/CodeGen/RISCV/rvv/fixed-vectors-fround-constrained-sdnode.ll`
+- `b13f799616939933373610c7458687ae88fa414d`: `llvm/test/CodeGen/RISCV/rvv/fround-costrained-sdnode.ll` -> `llvm/test/CodeGen/RISCV/rvv/fround-constrained-sdnode.ll`
+- `0afc884e874043bf5207d561ab82b107e8860d41`: `llvm/test/CodeGen/RISCV/rvv/trunc-sat-clip.ll` -> `llvm/test/CodeGen/RISCV/rvv/fixed-vectors-trunc-sat-clip.ll`
+
+## Isolation
+Main base 05fb8af658ad55d79726e4815bedddde8fed2175. Snapshot 79aeb169e7af preserves existing dirty lit.sh, integrate.py and test_harness.py; notes/19/H001-base.patch records prerequisite differences. Apply ONLY the subsequent H001 implementation delta after independent review, not snapshot. No main checkout or LLVM test modifications. Mapping and real report live in this worktree steps/19.
