@@ -0,0 +1,14 @@
+## What upstream changed
+Harness defect, not an LLVM change: lit.sh returned before writing lit_diff when gtest failed; integrate.py compared only lit counts and could reuse stale reports. Main-clone base 05fb8af658ad; prerequisite snapshot 1cfbbeab584d records pre-existing conductor edits. Apply ONLY the subsequent H002 commit patch against the current harness, retaining H001 rename changes.
+
+## Why this is equivalent
+No LLVM tests or expected results change. Every executed gtest is recorded by classname/name including shared TargetParser suites. Failure details are preserved verbatim in report.unit.failures. Integration requires valid positive inventory, no lost unit cases, no new lit problem identities or failing unit cases, and strict combined shrink unless already green. Unit JSON/process disagreement and unknown build failures reject. Fresh output removal prevents accidental stale reports. Missing unit baseline evidence requires regeneration; legacy lit-only baseline is not accepted for landing.
+
+## What breaks if this is wrong
+A unit regression or stale report could incorrectly allow a change to land. Failed assertions within a still-failing test deliberately do not count as improvement: E004 alone remains rejected if PrintExtensions stays failed. E004 plus reviewed T005 should be validated together. This measures complete unit test cases, never text/padding edit distance.
+
+## How verified
+python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -v: 21 tests PASS. bash -n scripts/lit.sh PASS. New tests exercise valid failed unit diagnostic report emission, missing/zero unit JSON, mismatched process status, unchanged failures, exchanged failures, strict improvement, coverage loss, legacy baseline rejection, stale integration output, and unknown nonzero build status. Independent review required before application. H001 owns baseline rename mapping; H002 edits separate lit_diff imports/options/report augmentation and lit.sh unit handling.
+
+## Upstream reference
+No LLVM upstream commit applies: this fixes harness control flow and evidence validation without changing LLVM source or expected results. Harness reference: scripts/lit.sh unit-process failure handling and scripts/integrate.py combined lit/unit gate, based on main harness commit 05fb8af658ad and prerequisite snapshot 1cfbbeab584d. The combined H001/H002 candidate adds this required section to resolve the independent H002 review rejection; implementation is unchanged by this documentation correction.
